// @corpus: rejected
// @id: R-048
// @category: title outside the top of a page's view
// @rule: PW5030
// @invariant: title_misplaced
// @charter: §15.6 test 14, §17.4
// @milestone: 14
// @expect-error: `<title>` in the view `Heading` titles every page that composes it
// @expect-error: a title is the page's: once, at the top of its view, written as text and values
//
// A title is what a page says it is (ADR-0183). One written in a view would
// title every page the view is composed into, the same, and a page that
// composed two would have two titles, of which the browser shows the first.

module store.heading

view Heading() !{} {
    <title>Store</title>
    <h1>Store</h1>
}
